NNAAMMEE
       EVP_MAC-KMAC, EVP_MAC-KMAC128, EVP_MAC-KMAC256 - The KMAC EVP_MAC
       implementations

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       Support for computing KMAC MACs through the EEVVPP__MMAACC API.

   IIddeennttiittyy
       These implementations are identified with one of these names and
       properties, to be used with EEVVPP__MMAACC__ffeettcchh(()):

       "KMAC-128", "provider=default" or "provider=fips"
       "KMAC-256", "provider=default" or "provider=fips"

   SSuuppppoorrtteedd ppaarraammeetteerrss
       The   general   description   of  these  parameters  can  be  found  in
       "PARAMETERS" in EEVVPP__MMAACC(3).

       All  these  parameters  can  be  set   with   EEVVPP__MMAACC__CCTTXX__sseett__ppaarraammss(()).
       Furthermore,    the    "size"   parameter   can   be   retrieved   with
       EEVVPP__MMAACC__CCTTXX__ggeett__ppaarraammss(()),  or  with  EEVVPP__MMAACC__CCTTXX__ggeett__mmaacc__ssiizzee(()).    The
       length  of  the  "size"  parameter  should not exceed that of a ssiizzee__tt.
       Likewise,  the   "block‐size"   parameter   can   be   retrieved   with
       EEVVPP__MMAACC__CCTTXX__ggeett__ppaarraammss(()), or with EEVVPP__MMAACC__CCTTXX__ggeett__bblloocckk__ssiizzee(()).

       "key" (OOSSSSLL__MMAACC__PPAARRAAMM__KKEEYY) <octet string>
           Sets the MAC key.  Setting this parameter is identical to passing a
           _k_e_y  to  EEVVPP__MMAACC__iinniitt(3).  The length of the key (in bytes) must be
           in the range 4...512.

       "custom" (OOSSSSLL__MMAACC__PPAARRAAMM__CCUUSSTTOOMM) <octet string>
           Sets the custom value.  It is an optional value with a length of at
           most 512 bytes, and is empty by default.

       "size" (OOSSSSLL__MMAACC__PPAARRAAMM__SSIIZZEE) <unsigned integer>
           Sets the MAC size.  By default, it is 16 for "KMAC-128" and 32  for
           "KMAC-256".

       "block‐size" (OOSSSSLL__MMAACC__PPAARRAAMM__SSIIZZEE) <unsigned integer>
           Gets  the MAC block size.  By default, it is 168 for "KMAC-128" and
           136 for "KMAC-256".

       "xof" (OOSSSSLL__MMAACC__PPAARRAAMM__XXOOFF) <integer>
           The "xof" parameter value is expected to be 1 or 0. Use 1 to enable
           XOF mode.  The default value is 0.

       The  "custom"  parameter  must  be  set  as  part  of  or  before   the
       EEVVPP__MMAACC__iinniitt(()) call.  The "xof" and "size" parameters can be set at any
       time before EEVVPP__MMAACC__ffiinnaall(()).  The "key" parameter is set as part of the
       EEVVPP__MMAACC__iinniitt(()) call, but can be set before it instead.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
         #include <openssl/evp.h>
         #include <openssl/params.h>

         static int do_kmac(const unsigned char *in, size_t in_len,
                            const unsigned char *key, size_t key_len,
                            const unsigned char *custom, size_t custom_len,
                            int xof_enabled, unsigned char *out, int out_len)
         {
             EVP_MAC_CTX *ctx = NULL;
             EVP_MAC *mac = NULL;
             OSSL_PARAM params[4], *p;
             int ret = 0;
             size_t l = 0;

             mac = EVP_MAC_fetch(NULL, "KMAC-128", NULL);
             if (mac == NULL)
                 goto err;
             ctx = EVP_MAC_CTX_new(mac);
             /* The mac can be freed after it is used by EVP_MAC_CTX_new */
             EVP_MAC_free(mac);
             if (ctx == NULL)
                 goto err;

             /*
              * Setup parameters required before calling EVP_MAC_init()
              * The parameters OSSL_MAC_PARAM_XOF and OSSL_MAC_PARAM_SIZE may also be
              * used at this point.
              */
             p = params;
             *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_MAC_PARAM_KEY,
                                                      (void *)key, key_len);
             if (custom != NULL && custom_len != 0)
               *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_MAC_PARAM_CUSTOM,
                                                        (void *)custom, custom_len);
             *p = OSSL_PARAM_construct_end();
             if (!EVP_MAC_CTX_set_params(ctx, params))
                 goto err;

             if (!EVP_MAC_init(ctx))
                 goto err;

             /*
              * Note: the following optional parameters can be set any time
              * before EVP_MAC_final().
              */
             p = params;
             *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_int(OSSL_MAC_PARAM_XOF, &xof_enabled);
             *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_int(OSSL_MAC_PARAM_SIZE, &out_len);
             *p = OSSL_PARAM_construct_end();
             if (!EVP_MAC_CTX_set_params(ctx, params))
                 goto err;

             /* The update may be called multiple times here for streamed input */
             if (!EVP_MAC_update(ctx, in, in_len))
                 goto err;
             if (!EVP_MAC_final(ctx, out, &l, out_len))
                 goto err;
             ret = 1;
         err:
             EVP_MAC_CTX_free(ctx);
             return ret;
         }

